    "question": {
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $A$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} && R_{2}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -5 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots. In particular, the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $3$rd columns.",
      ":question/id": "8f90b51b-299e-594d-82a8-5e60c316e603",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "112190eb-ed6d-5ce2-a62f-9c16da6756a3",
